WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.302
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:04.804
[ Cheers and applause ]
And everybody watching at home.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.840
Thank you.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.508
Well, guys, the weekend
kicks off

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:11.711
the unofficial start of summer.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.545
That's right,
happy Memorial Day.

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:17.750
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.352
-Happy Memorial Day
to all of you,

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.519
except for that guy
in your office

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.588
who sent a work e-mail
at 4:59 p.m.

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:24.757
You go, "No, we're not reading
it, Carl."

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.125
I have a feeling people

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.627
are going to really
let loose this weekend.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.828
Don't you have that feeling?

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.930
[ Cheers ]

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.165
By this time tomorrow,
the cornhole boards

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:35.502
will just be two guys passed out
with their mouths open.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:39.905
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:41.007
Listen to this.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.376
According to AAA,
nearly 40 million people

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:47.680
are expected to travel 50 miles
or more this weekend.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.149
When asked where they're
going, everyone said, "Anywhere.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.818
Literally. Anywhere else."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:54.587
Meanwhile, with so
many people traveling

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:58.024
this weekend, gas prices
are expected to skyrocket.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.758
Yeah, the bad news is gas
is expensive.

00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:01.761
But good news is you'll have
something to talk about

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.429
with your father-in-law.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.132
"Can you believe
how expensive the gas --"

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.267
Gas is so expensive,
when I filled up this morning,

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.468
a guy in a tux was like,

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.571
"Might I recommend
the Sunoco 92?"

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:14.606
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.606 --> 00:01:17.209
"Excellent choice,
Mr. Fallon."

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.878
Speaking of traveling,
a new survey finds

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.312
that the majority of Americans

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:24.083
won't take a road trip
without the perfect playlist.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:27.353
And 35% said they'd turn the car
around if they didn't have one.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.288
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:32.025
What's more troubling is only 8%
said they'd turn the car around

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.492
if they forgot
one of their kids.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:34.694
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.697
-"Ah, he doesn't listen
to my music anyway."

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.732
Yeah, you spend days
making the perfect playlist,

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.400
then you spend the whole trip
trying to connect

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.635
your phone
to the car's Bluetooth.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.370
It's really fun.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.106
"Alright, everyone turn
their Bluetooth off!

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.907
Everyone turn --
Now I got to pull over.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.008
Here we go.
Then we're gonna have fun.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.908
Then we're gonna have fun.

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:52.678
Everyone turn it off!"

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:54.813
Get this -- according to
the National Hot Dog

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.316
and Sausage Council...

00:01:56.316 --> 00:02:01.787
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.989
...73% of Americans believe
that a barbecue

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:07.459
is not complete
without hot dogs.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:08.861
I think the bigger story here
is that we have

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.030
a National Hot Dog
and Sausage Council.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.431
[ Laughter ]
-Come on.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:13.733
-Send me a T-shirt, man.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.634
-Number one.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.503
-A lot of Americans are going
to barbecues this weekend.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.105
And sometimes you have
good barbecues.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.473
Sometimes you have bad ones.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.575
So we actually came up
with some clues, some warnings,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.177
to help you guys realize
that you're at a bad one.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:27.146
So if you see this --
For example, if you're at --

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.714
you're at a bad barbecue
if your neighbor's

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:31.017
wearing an apron that says,
"French kiss the chef."

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.919
[ Audience ohs ]
That's disgust-- that's gross.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.353
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.155
Here we go, this warning here.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.791
A 911 call includes
the words "grandpa,"

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.460
"lawn dart," and "impale."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.696
That means you're
at a bad barbecue.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.365
-That's a bad one?
-This is a bad one, yeah.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.432
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.800
Here's another warning --
bad one.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.336
The neighbor's teenage son
sneaking shots of lighter fluid.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.037
-Okay.

00:02:52.037 --> 00:02:55.241
-Don't have him burp
by the grill. Yeah.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.608
Also, here's another warning.

00:02:56.608 --> 00:02:57.977
Good news -- there's beer pong.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.413
Bad news -- it's with
Natty Light Sour Seltzer.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.314
[ Audience ohs ]
-Oh.

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:04.417
-That was a mixed reaction.
Someone out there likes it.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.586
[ Laughter ]
Someone likes that.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.120
-Is that real?
-I'm not afraid of it.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.755
I'll try it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:12.058
And, finally, warning,
a guy with seven fingers says,

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.692
"Who wants to shoot off
some fireworks?"

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.295
Just some warning signs.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.997
Just a couple.
If you see those, just know.

00:03:18.997 --> 00:03:21.000
Well, changing gears, today
Senate Republicans

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.736
voted to block
the January 6th commission

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.971
that would investigate
the Capitol riots.

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:27.840
[ Audience booing ]

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.142
After the vote, Republicans
said they'll gladly explain

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.945
their decision in an upcoming
QAnon -- I mean Q&amp;A.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:38.250
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.852
Thank you.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.254
That's a great crowd.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.955
Senate Republicans said they'd
rather investigate

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:44.424
something more important, like

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.358
why wasn't Paul Rudd
in the "Friends" reunion?

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:48.660
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.929
That makes more sense.

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:52.131
Here's some good news.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.133
Right here this weekend
all New York beaches

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.569
will be open,
and vaccine buses

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.604
will be stationed
on a few of them.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:02.074
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.510
And just to make sure
they attract a crowd,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.013
all the vaccine buses
will play the Mr. Softee jingle.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.215
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.849
Yeah, the vaccine buses
are a great idea

00:04:10.849 --> 00:04:12.852
because when they're done,
they can just toss the needles

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.086
on the beach
with all the others.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:15.988
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.257
"Hey, what are you gonna do?"

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.293
[ Laughter ]
"We're at the beach!"

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.294
-"Hey, I'm with
the Sausage Council!"

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.997
-"That's right. We work
for the Sausage Council.

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:27.133
What he said."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.835
Another sign that
we're returning to normal --

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:31.971 line:0%
Costco is bringing back
their free samples.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:36.576 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.478
Don't worry, though.
They're still being careful.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.713
Now a Costco employee
will just slingshot

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.349
a cheese cube into your mouth.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.084
Some more business news --
American Airlines

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:48.153
just announced that they're
partnering with Rosetta Stone

00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:51.257
to offer language courses
to passengers during flights.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.491
-Ooh.

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.193
-You think someone kicking
your seat is tough,

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.262
imagine sitting next to some guy
sounding out French

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.663
for six hours.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.566
"Bonj-- bonjoi-- Bonjoar?

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:04.236
Aurevware? Aurvware. Aurvwar.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.672
Aurvwar. Aurvwar.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:09.141
Aurvwar. Bonjar.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:12.010
Bonjar. Aurvoir. Jonbar."

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.347
John Bar Jarvoir, everyone.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.048
Love him.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:17.983
That's right.
The airline's also offering

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.285
courses like photography.

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:21.754
So flying isn't awkward enough.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.490
Just wait till a stranger's
snapping photos of you sleeping.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.125
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.693
"You looked
beautiful and peaceful."

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:30.128
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.128 --> 00:05:31.430
Well, this made me laugh.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.299
Yesterday a CNN reporter
was preparing for a live shot

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.200
when he realized
a cicada was on him.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.636
Take a look at this.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.237
-Am I going to be in the --
in the same block out of this

00:05:39.237 --> 00:05:41.074
or going to take a break?

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.642
Okay.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:46.378
[ Audience ohs ]

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:47.547
Oh!

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:49.315
Oh, my God!

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:52.351
[Bleep]

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:54.353
[Bleep] cicada.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.656
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:58.491
-Everyone in the control room
was like --

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.126
they just sat back there like,
"Let's just see how this --"

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.527
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.695
"Let's see how this plays out.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:04.429
Let's not say anything."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.429 --> 00:06:07.032
Speaking of cicadas,
a photographer in Virginia

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:09.167
has recently picked up
an interesting new hobby.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:10.169
Check this out.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.272
-We started with
my son's fire truck.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:17.376
I decided to do
a cicada rock band.

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:19.045
This cicada is doing archery.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.914
[ Laughter ]
This cicada was lifting.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.850
Look, Ping-Pong.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:30.156
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:33.458
-Okay, so clearly not everyone
made it through quarantine okay.

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:36.528
[ Laughter ]
-Ping-Pong.

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:39.698
-Guys, finally, as I mentioned,
Monday is Memorial Day,

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:42.001
and people are excited
to go to barbecues again.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:43.736
I love a good
old-fashioned potluck,

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:44.803
where everyone brings a side.

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:46.205
But there's nothing worse

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:48.641
than when no one
wants to eat your side.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:51.377
Here, let me explain with
a "Tonight Show" tiny song.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:54.580
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.984 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:01.687
♪ It's my first barbecue
in two years ♪

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:05.858
♪ Can't wait to see my friends
and crack some beers ♪

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:09.362
♪ Dave brought fruit salad,
Ann brought rum lemonade ♪

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:15.067
♪ But no one's touched the thing
that I made ♪

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:18.837
♪ Somebody eat my carrot slaw ♪

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:22.909
♪ Please somebody eat
my carrot slaw ♪

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:26.412
♪ Heard someone ask, "Hey,
what's that supposed to be?" ♪

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:30.349
♪ Glad my grandma's not
'cause it's her recipe ♪

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:34.120
♪ Somebody eat my carrot slaw ♪

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.890
♪ Somebody eat my carrot slaw ♪

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:43.395
♪ No one put it on their plate
even though I'm right here ♪

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:47.099
♪ Saying, "Doesn't
this look great? ♪

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:49.802
♪ Now I'm leaving the party ♪

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:52.771
♪ Can't look people in the eye ♪

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:55.141
♪ So I'll just throw it
in my freezer ♪

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:58.043
♪ Till the fourth of July ♪

00:07:58.043 --> 00:08:01.680
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.282
Two, three, four.

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:09.121 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.222
We have a great show.

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:11.557
Give it up for the Roots,
everybody.

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.158
[ Cheers and applause ]

